From 03e60cf0894fb0ba4e7f6e9c8d098725a0ab315d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel Mac Builds <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:54:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] deps: enable OIDN's Metal device only on Apple Silicon

openimagedenoise.cmake sets -DOIDN_DEVICE_METAL=ON for all APPLE builds,
with no architecture gate. On x86_64 that is wrong twice over.

It cannot work at runtime. OIDN's own README lists its supported Metal
hardware as "Apple silicon GPUs (M1 and newer)". An Intel Mac has an AMD
or Intel GPU, so the Metal backend it produces could never be
instantiated.

And it cannot even be built without full Xcode. Compiling the Metal
kernels shells out to the Metal shader compiler, which since Xcode 16 is
a separately downloaded component and is absent from Command Line Tools
entirely:

  xcrun: error: unable to find utility "metal"
  make[5]: *** [.../OpenImageDenoise_device_metal.dir/metal_kernels.air] Error 72
  make[2]: *** [.../external_openimagedenoise-build] Error 2

That failure is fatal to the whole dependency build, at 96%, for a
backend the target hardware can never use.

Gate it on BLENDER_PLATFORM_ARM, which options.cmake sets only when
CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES is arm64. Apple Silicon is unaffected. The
x86_64 path sets OIDN_DEVICE_CPU=ON explicitly -- that is already OIDN's
default, but stating it keeps the intent legible: CPU is the only
denoising device an Intel Mac can use.
---
 .../cmake/openimagedenoise.cmake              | 27 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimagedenoise.cmake b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimagedenoise.cmake
index 2ddcbd63..228240c3 100644
--- a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimagedenoise.cmake
+++ b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/openimagedenoise.cmake
@@ -11,10 +11,29 @@ set(OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS
   -DPython_EXECUTABLE=${PYTHON_BINARY}
 )
 if(APPLE)
-  set(OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS
-    ${OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS}
-    -DOIDN_DEVICE_METAL=ON
-  )
+  # OIDN's Metal device targets "Apple silicon GPUs (M1 and newer)" only -- an
+  # Intel Mac's AMD or Intel GPU is not on its supported list, so the backend
+  # could never be instantiated at runtime there. Building it anyway hard-
+  # requires the Metal shader compiler, which is a separate Xcode component and
+  # is absent under Command Line Tools, taking the whole dependency build down:
+  #
+  #   xcrun: error: unable to find utility "metal"
+  #   make[5]: *** [.../OpenImageDenoise_device_metal.dir/metal_kernels.air] Error 72
+  #
+  # So enable Metal only on Apple Silicon. OIDN_DEVICE_CPU defaults to ON, but
+  # set it explicitly on the x86_64 path so the intent is visible: CPU is the
+  # only denoising device an Intel Mac can use.
+  if(BLENDER_PLATFORM_ARM)
+    set(OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS
+      ${OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS}
+      -DOIDN_DEVICE_METAL=ON
+    )
+  else()
+    set(OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS
+      ${OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS}
+      -DOIDN_DEVICE_CPU=ON
+    )
+  endif()
 else()
   set(OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS
     ${OIDN_EXTRA_ARGS}
-- 
